 ## Operating characteristics
--   **Time Complexity**: $O(N)$, where $N$ is the number of voxels, as each voxel is processed once.
--   **Memory Complexity**: $O(N)$ for the output mesh, potentially higher than standard MT due to the 5-tetrahedron split.
--   **Strengths**: Provides additional planes of symmetry and generates open spaces around points outside the surface, which can be beneficial for certain visualization tasks [S1, S2]. It avoids the ambiguity of standard cube slicing by ensuring consistent diagonal interpolation [S1, S2].
--   **Limitations**: The alternating vertex density results in a mesh that varies slightly depending on position [S1, S2]. It may produce artificial "bumps" due to face diagonal interpolation [S1, S2]. It requires additional calculations for diagonals across cube faces compared to Dual Contouring [S1, S2]. It does not handle the "near points inside surface" case, which may require Manifold Dual Contouring modifications [S1, S2].
